[252.846465, "o", "overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  63: Site visit #134 to fixed assets captured mailbox exports showing how capital project capitalization correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  65: Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  67: Memo WP-1725 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  69: Site visit #521 to fixed assets captured mailbox exports showing how capital project capitalization correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  71: The committee p"]
