[429.571969, "o", "13:(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n15:transaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n16:same rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n17:`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n18:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n19:notice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n20:by notice_id ascending.\r\n26:Risk assessment WP-5486 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n28:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n30:Memo WP-5276 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalizat"]
[429.572016, "o", "ion. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n32:Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n36:Follow-up #632 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n"]
[429.572045, "o", "38:In July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n"]
